    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0335" n="236" xml:id="pg236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/775: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Muccio</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-22T10:00:00-04:00">June 22, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. Bautista Saavedra arrested and deported night of June 20, many other
                    Saavedrists or Republican Socialists arrested.</p>
                <p>Chief of Army Staff in manifesto dated June 21 accuses Saavedrists of subversive
                    activities against the realization of the aims of the May 17 movement, ratifies
                    confidence of the army in the military members of the Junta, and gives full
                    freedom to the President to complete the Junta and continue carrying out the
                    minimum program of the Government.</p>
                <p>Colonel Toro declared to press last evening that three civilians would be
                    retained on Junta in personal capacity not representing any political party.
                    Personnel of Junta not yet announced though Finot<anchor n="19" xml:id="d205-f1"
                    /> is mentioned for Minister of Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d205-f1" n="19" xml:id="d205-f1-content">
                <p>Enrique Finot.</p>
            </note>
